== 2.10 Chapter 2 Practice Drill — 30 Questions

30 questions graded in the order the CBT engine is likely to meet them. Allow 33 minutes; the key and a full solution for every question follow.

#mcq(1, [A cross between two organisms that differ in one pair of contrasting characters is a],
  [test cross],
  [dihybrid cross],
  [monohybrid cross],
  [back cross]
)

#mcq(2, [A Punnett square is used to],
  [measure the height of a plant],
  [count chromosomes],
  [show the possible combinations of gametes and their offspring],
  [show a family tree]
)

#mcq(3, [The expected phenotypic ratio from a cross between two heterozygotes (Tt × Tt) is],
  [3 : 1],
  [1 : 2 : 1],
  [1 : 1],
  [9 : 3 : 3 : 1]
)

#mcq(4, [If a tall pea plant is crossed with a short one and all the offspring are tall, the tall parent is most probably],
  [homozygous recessive],
  [homozygous dominant],
  [haploid],
  [heterozygous]
)

#mcq(5, [A test cross is made between an organism of unknown genotype and one that is],
  [homozygous recessive],
  [heterozygous],
  [haploid],
  [homozygous dominant]
)

#mcq(6, [The probability that a heterozygous parent passes on its recessive allele is],
  [1/2],
  [1/4],
  [1],
  [0]
)

#mcq(7, [In a cross Tt × tt, the expected ratio of phenotypes is],
  [3 : 1],
  [1 : 1],
  [9 : 3 : 3 : 1],
  [1 : 2 : 1]
)

#mcq(8, [The chance that two heterozygous parents both pass on the recessive allele is],
  [1/8],
  [1/2],
  [1/4],
  [1/16]
)

#mcq(9, [A dihybrid cross between two heterozygotes (AaBb × AaBb) gives a phenotypic ratio of],
  [1 : 2 : 1],
  [3 : 1],
  [9 : 3 : 3 : 1],
  [1 : 1 : 1 : 1]
)

#mcq(10, [Two genes that are carried on the same chromosome are said to be],
  [linked],
  [epistatic],
  [sex-linked],
  [codominant]
)

#mcq(11, [The ABO blood group is an example of],
  [polygenic inheritance],
  [complete dominance only],
  [sex linkage],
  [multiple alleles and codominance]
)

#mcq(12, [A man of blood group AB marries a woman of group O. The possible blood groups of their children are],
  [AB and O only],
  [A and B only],
  [O only],
  [A, B, AB and O]
)

#mcq(13, [A man of blood group O marries a woman of group AB. Which blood group is impossible in their children?],
  [A],
  [AB],
  [B],
  [O]
)

#mcq(14, [Haemophilia is inherited as a],
  [recessive allele on the Y chromosome],
  [codominant allele],
  [dominant autosomal allele],
  [recessive sex-linked allele on the X chromosome]
)

#mcq(15, [A colour-blind man marries a woman who is homozygous normal. Their sons will be],
  [all colour-blind],
  [half colour-blind],
  [all normal],
  [all carriers]
)

#mcq(16, [A carrier woman (X^B^X^b^) marries a normal man. The chance that a son is colour-blind is],
  [0],
  [3/4],
  [1/4],
  [1/2]
)

#mcq(17, [The sex of a child is determined at],
  [the third month of pregnancy],
  [birth],
  [the moment the sperm fuses with the egg],
  [puberty]
)

#mcq(18, [A characteristic that appears in every generation, in both sexes, is most likely],
  [Y-linked],
  [autosomal dominant],
  [sex-linked recessive],
  [autosomal recessive]
)

#mcq(19, [In a pedigree, a shaded square represents],
  [an affected female],
  [an affected male],
  [an unaffected male],
  [a carrier female]
)

#mcq(20, [Incomplete dominance is shown when the heterozygote],
  [looks exactly like the dominant homozygote],
  [has an intermediate phenotype],
  [is sterile],
  [looks exactly like the recessive homozygote]
)

#mcq(21, [In incomplete dominance, the F2 phenotypic ratio from two pink parents is],
  [3 : 1],
  [1 : 2 : 1],
  [1 : 1],
  [9 : 3 : 3 : 1]
)

#mcq(22, [A woman who is a carrier of haemophilia is],
  [homozygous dominant],
  [unable to have children],
  [affected by the disease],
  [unaffected but can pass the allele on]
)

#mcq(23, [Two parents are both heterozygous for a recessive condition. The chance that their child is affected is],
  [3/4],
  [1/2],
  [1/4],
  [0]
)

#mcq(24, [The probability rule used when two independent events must both happen is the],
  [law of segregation],
  [product rule],
  [law of linkage],
  [sum rule]
)

#mcq(25, [The probability rule used when either of two mutually exclusive events can happen is the],
  [product rule],
  [law of independent assortment],
  [law of dominance],
  [sum rule]
)

#mcq(26, [A cross between a heterozygote and a homozygous recessive gives 50 tall and 50 short offspring. The heterozygote was],
  [TT],
  [tt],
  [Tt],
  [T]
)

#mcq(27, [A man and a woman are both carriers of sickle-cell anaemia. The chance that a child is a carrier is],
  [1/2],
  [0],
  [3/4],
  [1/4]
)

#mcq(28, [Which cross can produce a child of blood group O from two parents of group A?],
  [I^A^I^A^ × I^A^I^A^],
  [I^A^i × I^B^i],
  [I^A^i × I^A^i],
  [I^A^I^A^ × I^A^i]
)

#mcq(29, [A trait that appears only in males and is passed from father to son is most likely],
  [X-linked recessive],
  [autosomal recessive],
  [autosomal dominant],
  [Y-linked]
)

#mcq(30, [In a monohybrid cross, the F1 generation is obtained by crossing],
  [the two parental varieties],
  [two F1 individuals],
  [an F1 with a parent],
  [two recessives]
)

